00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:21.980
- [Zenobia Dobson:] Let me call his coach to see if he can set it up.

00:00:22.105 --> 00:00:23.189
- All right, well, I appreciate that.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:24.024
Talk soon.

00:00:24.649 --> 00:00:32.490
♪♪♪

00:00:48.465 --> 00:00:49.382
- [Zack Dobson:] I still to this day,

00:00:49.424 --> 00:00:51.760
I just don't understand, like, why everything happened.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:57.057
Cuz, like, we was literally chillin'. Like, wasn't doin' nothin’.

00:00:59.017 --> 00:01:01.186
- [Anthony:] Three years ago in Knoxville, Tennessee,

00:01:01.686 --> 00:01:05.273
Zack Dobson and his brother Zaevion were just laughing on the porch.

00:01:06.274 --> 00:01:09.152
Zae died. Zack ran.

00:01:10.195 --> 00:01:12.906
He's tackling an all-too-familiar situation. 

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:15.575
Movin' on from tragedy back home,

00:01:16.451 --> 00:01:18.787
makin' moves to be a better player and a better man,

00:01:19.329 --> 00:01:20.789
all with a smile on his face. 

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:26.878
- [Zenobia:] This is Texas Avenue.

00:01:27.879 --> 00:01:34.636
We’re comin’ up on the house that Zack, Zaevion and Markastin were raised up in.

00:01:35.011 --> 00:01:35.762
Hey!

00:01:39.307 --> 00:01:40.558
- [Markastin Taylor:] Twenty-one sixteen.

00:01:40.558 --> 00:01:42.102
- [Zenobia:] Twenty-one sixteen—that’s it.

00:01:42.644 --> 00:01:44.395
That’s where the boys were raised up at.

00:01:44.395 --> 00:01:46.523
On the side of the house, that was the football field.

00:01:46.523 --> 00:01:46.731
[Laughing]

00:01:46.731 --> 00:01:47.190
- [Markastin:] Yup.

00:01:47.315 --> 00:01:48.525
- [Zenobia:] That was their field.

00:01:48.733 --> 00:01:50.944
- [Markastin:] That’s actually where the ground started.

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:51.861
- [Zenobia:] Hmm.

00:01:52.487 --> 00:01:55.865
- [Markastin:] Zaevion would—he would push Zack to his limits. 

00:01:56.199 --> 00:01:56.783
- [Zenobia:] Hmm!

00:01:57.075 --> 00:01:57.742
- [Markastin:] He would.

00:01:58.159 --> 00:02:00.578
♪♪♪

00:02:01.079 --> 00:02:03.123
- [Zack:] He was, like, my little big brother basically. 

00:02:03.581 --> 00:02:06.000
If I’m there, Zaevion’s there, or he’s not far.

00:02:06.376 --> 00:02:07.836
It’s Zack and Zaevion always.

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:10.839
- [Zenobia:] I mean, ridin’ their bikes, 

00:02:11.214 --> 00:02:13.758
goin’ to the playground, goin’ to the basketball court.

00:02:14.259 --> 00:02:15.260
- Well, I’m from the hood.

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:17.971
There was bad stuff goin’ on in the neighborhood, like shootings and everything.

00:02:17.971 --> 00:02:21.599
But, I mean, we made a way to really, like, stay away from all that.

00:02:21.599 --> 00:02:24.435
Like, we was just doin’ our own thing—in our own world.

00:02:26.437 --> 00:02:30.024
It was the last day of school. It was break. Then we went to the Fulton game. 

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:33.778
So we go home. I checked in with my mama. Checked in—everything was cool.

00:02:34.445 --> 00:02:38.074
So we end up walkin’ on the back street all the way up this long street.

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:41.536
We got up there. We just, we just chillin’. 

00:02:41.536 --> 00:02:44.747
Then all of the sudden, we just see people walkin’ towards us in the street. 

00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:49.419
And then I get up, cuz, like, I know everybody in the community.

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:51.462
Like, everybody know me, my mama and my brother.  

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:53.590
So I’m like, “OK, this ain’t, this ain’t about to happen.”

00:02:53.756 --> 00:02:55.258
As soon as I took a step off the porch, 

00:02:55.258 --> 00:02:58.219
as soon as I—as soon as my foot touched the other step, they start shootin’.

00:03:01.472 --> 00:03:03.725
That’s when I get to panicking. Just panicking. 

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:08.021
And I, I just took off. I just took off runnin’. I just took off runnin’.

00:03:08.605 --> 00:03:09.397
I just took off runnin’.

00:03:11.983 --> 00:03:13.818
- A developing story in Knoxville

00:03:13.818 --> 00:03:16.529
- Tennessee is mourning a high school football player.

00:03:16.571 --> 00:03:19.115
- Sophomore standout who had star potential

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:20.867
- Who was killed by a group of gunmen.

00:03:20.867 --> 00:03:22.660
- Randomly targeted in a shooting

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:23.453
- Shot dead.

00:03:23.453 --> 00:03:25.914
- Zaevion’s story has dominated social media

00:03:25.997 --> 00:03:28.082
- The teenager who’s being hailed a hero

00:03:28.124 --> 00:03:30.168
- Died trying to shield three girls

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:31.252
- Three young girls

00:03:31.252 --> 00:03:32.962
- In a spasm of violence

00:03:32.962 --> 00:03:37.217
- [Screaming] Lord, I need you! Oh, have mercy!

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:40.887
- He wasn’t in the wrong place at the wrong time. He hadn’t made a bad decision.

00:03:41.596 --> 00:03:44.807
He was exactly where any other kid would be.

00:03:45.183 --> 00:03:48.144
Your kid. My kids.

00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:51.689
He gave his life to save theirs.

00:03:52.357 --> 00:03:55.610
An act of heroism a lot bigger than anything

00:03:55.610 --> 00:03:57.737
we should ever expect from a 15-year-old.

00:03:59.322 --> 00:04:01.658
- [Zack:] It was, it was everywhere. It was everywhere.

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:05.370
And, like, I would say, like, I didn’t really, 

00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:10.708
I didn’t really get to grieve how I really wanted to because, like, it was just so much.

00:04:10.708 --> 00:04:16.381
Like, it was just the, the media and just how everything, how everything got, like—

00:04:17.882 --> 00:04:20.134
It was just, I really didn’t get the time to really grieve.

00:04:26.224 --> 00:04:27.686
♪♪♪

00:04:27.725 --> 00:04:30.436
- [Rob Black:] The moment Zack stepped on our campus,

00:04:30.478 --> 00:04:32.605
he was full of energy, very talented.

00:04:32.772 --> 00:04:37.151
Not very large in stature but played so much bigger than he really was.

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:41.698
- Zaevion followed him the year after. 

00:04:41.781 --> 00:04:44.242
- [Jermaine Buchannon:] Just because he didn’t want to be Zack’s little brother, 

00:04:44.242 --> 00:04:48.538
he pushed to make a name for himself, and I think that pushed Zack to continue.

00:04:48.705 --> 00:04:51.082
- [Black:] Zack was your skill guy. 

00:04:51.332 --> 00:04:54.502
Zaevion was more your bruiser linebacker-type guy.

00:04:55.003 --> 00:04:57.714
You could see between his freshman and sophomore year, 

00:04:57.714 --> 00:05:00.258
he figured out that this is not youth ball.

00:05:00.258 --> 00:05:02.885
- People think I got just good all of a sudden—nah, 

00:05:02.885 --> 00:05:05.471
I was really, like, workin’ out like crazy.

00:05:05.471 --> 00:05:08.891
Like, I was doin’ footwork drills almost every night.

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:11.227
Like, go outside—4 in the morning, 3 in the morning, 

00:05:11.227 --> 00:05:13.021
don’t matter—doin’ footwork drills.

00:05:13.146 --> 00:05:14.897
Be like, “You know what, I’m just gonna get this work.”

00:05:16.399 --> 00:05:18.151
- They called their room “the locker room.” 

00:05:18.776 --> 00:05:20.486
It smelt like a locker room as well.

00:05:20.653 --> 00:05:22.697
[Laughing]

00:05:22.697 --> 00:05:25.408
Our house in Lonsdale? Like, we had the most company.

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:26.951
It was like an open home. 

00:05:26.951 --> 00:05:29.162
Like, she never had a problem with any of our friends coming over.

00:05:29.287 --> 00:05:32.707
- [Zenobia:] It’s about love. I mean, that was my main thing.

00:05:32.832 --> 00:05:34.459
- A team mom of all team moms.

00:05:34.459 --> 00:05:37.670
I mean, she knew every player. They all knew her. 

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:40.006
They felt very comfortable around her.

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:42.592
- [Zenobia:] If they didn’t have their grades, they couldn’t play ball.

00:05:42.759 --> 00:05:45.178
If they didn’t have their homework, they couldn’t play ball.

00:05:45.428 --> 00:05:46.596
-  [Buchannon:] It taught ‘em hard work.

00:05:46.679 --> 00:05:49.223
- [Zack:] Here, run this. “Hit the fence,” that’s all he said. “Hit the fence.”

00:05:49.265 --> 00:05:51.601
- [Buchannon:] And along with hard work, we won.

00:05:51.601 --> 00:05:54.354
So that taught, along with hard work, comes success.

00:05:54.854 --> 00:05:57.273
And I think you carry that with you through life. 

00:05:58.608 --> 00:06:03.237
- I know that the jury, they heard me. I’m his brother—I was firsthand.

00:06:15.166 --> 00:06:16.834
I said: I’m not a gang member. I’m an athlete.

00:06:18.836 --> 00:06:20.755
- [Anthony:] Zae died a hero, and Zack 

00:06:20.755 --> 00:06:23.174
had to learn how to go to school without his best friend.

00:06:23.925 --> 00:06:25.802
How to play without his favorite teammate.

00:06:26.552 --> 00:06:27.887
How to live without his brother.

00:06:30.181 --> 00:06:32.141
And while Zack stood up to accept awards

00:06:32.141 --> 00:06:35.770
in Zae’s honor, he was rebuilding a life of his own.

00:06:36.854 --> 00:06:38.523
- [Zenobia:] He just felt responsible. 

00:06:39.941 --> 00:06:43.403
He thought that Zaevion was with him when he ran.

00:06:44.445 --> 00:06:47.698
- [Black:] I remember Zack not bein’ able to come to school for a while.

00:06:47.698 --> 00:06:51.369
I mean, it was affecting him in a, in a way that you would imagine it would.

00:06:51.369 --> 00:06:53.830
- I’ll never forget this: My coaches came to my house.

00:06:53.830 --> 00:06:58.918
- I felt like it was part of my job to go get him back here and try to support him.

00:06:59.168 --> 00:07:02.046
What a strong young man, and I know where that comes from.

00:07:02.046 --> 00:07:04.257
I know that comes from his mother.

00:07:05.216 --> 00:07:06.717
- Every day was a struggle. 

00:07:06.717 --> 00:07:09.470
He didn’t wanna go to school. He didn’t wanna get outta bed.

00:07:10.972 --> 00:07:11.431
[Sighing]

00:07:11.431 --> 00:07:12.807
He had a mental breakdown.

00:07:14.308 --> 00:07:17.019
- Like I—like, we did everything together, so he was always with me, 

00:07:17.019 --> 00:07:20.940
beside me, at breakfast with me, so I just, I was just not feelin’ it.

00:07:22.150 --> 00:07:24.735
Just—depression. I just didn’t feel the same.

00:07:25.153 --> 00:07:28.448
Like, I didn’t feel myself. I just felt dark. Just real dark.

00:07:28.823 --> 00:07:30.366
- [Chaton Mobley]: There were times when he just used to test me. 

00:07:30.366 --> 00:07:34.120
Be like, “Bro, I don’t know what to do. I don’t know, I don’t know what’s next for me.” 

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:37.081
He used to tell me how he used to stare, stare in his room, and nobody 

00:07:37.081 --> 00:07:39.375
used to be there, and he didn’t know how to handle 

00:07:39.375 --> 00:07:41.836
his brother not being there anymore—somebody he grew up with all his life. 

00:07:42.378 --> 00:07:43.796
- [Zenobia:] We were at a breaking point. 

00:07:44.755 --> 00:07:48.092
But that support and the love that we had for each other—we just 

00:07:48.092 --> 00:07:51.637
grabbed each other a little tighter...and held on.

00:07:52.555 --> 00:07:56.017
He didn’t give up, even though he wanted to. 

00:07:56.726 --> 00:07:59.562
And he was at the point of his life where he could have.

00:08:00.271 --> 00:08:04.025
He could have got revenge. He could have been bitter.

00:08:05.318 --> 00:08:07.695
But he wanted to rep his brother in a different way.

00:08:10.323 --> 00:08:13.284
- [Zack:] It was either the night or the next night that it happened—I, I texted 

00:08:13.284 --> 00:08:17.079
my coach, and I was like, “I wanna change my number. I wanna be 24.”

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:20.416
- “I wanna wear Zaevion’s number. I wanna be No. 24 next year.”

00:08:20.541 --> 00:08:24.545
- He said, “Mama, I mean, I know that’s what Zaevion wanted.

00:08:24.879 --> 00:08:29.759
I’m gonna live his legacy. I’m gonna do what it takes for my brother.”

00:08:33.596 --> 00:08:36.474
- [Cheering]

00:08:37.517 --> 00:08:39.894
- [Zack:] He wanted to be a coach. He wanted to be a coach.

00:08:40.061 --> 00:08:42.772
That’s one thing—I will never forget that. He wanted to be a coach.

00:08:42.813 --> 00:08:44.565
He would always tell me he wanted to pick my school.

00:08:44.565 --> 00:08:45.900
I was gonna straight up let him pick it. 

00:08:46.234 --> 00:08:49.612
He was the football guru, so I’m just, I’m gonna let him do it. That’s you.

00:08:49.820 --> 00:08:53.533
There’s one thing he’d say: “If a school offer you, they’re

00:08:53.533 --> 00:08:55.618
gonna offer me too, cuz I’m your brother.”

00:08:56.160 --> 00:08:59.288
- [Anthony:] Now Zack is out here at Middle Tennessee State University—

00:08:59.956 --> 00:09:02.250
the first in his family on a college scholarship,

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:04.126
playing wide receiver,

00:09:04.585 --> 00:09:05.920
wearing his brother’s number,

00:09:06.504 --> 00:09:08.214
making a name for himself.

00:09:08.714 --> 00:09:11.175
- [Coach Rick Stockstill:] I think the thing that, that stands out 

00:09:11.175 --> 00:09:14.554
the most about Zack is just his overall athleticism. 

00:09:15.221 --> 00:09:18.015
- [Zack] People still recruit small guys. I mean, if you can play ball, you can play ball.

00:09:18.182 --> 00:09:20.935
- [Stockstill:] The ability to play multiple positions. 

00:09:20.935 --> 00:09:22.687
Because he played running back. 

00:09:22.687 --> 00:09:25.106
He played wide receiver. He played defensive back.

00:09:25.231 --> 00:09:26.524
He returned kicks. 

00:09:27.149 --> 00:09:29.235
- [Mobley:] We never thought it would come true until senior year

00:09:29.235 --> 00:09:33.072
when we realized that Middle Tennessee had both—recruited us both, 

00:09:33.072 --> 00:09:34.865
and they both liked us, really both as players.

00:09:35.616 --> 00:09:37.827
Once they offered me, I knew they was gonna offer him eventually. 

00:09:38.286 --> 00:09:42.373
- [Markastin:] As soon as he got the news that he was goin’ to school, his, 

00:09:42.665 --> 00:09:45.293
his expressions and everything just changed, and then 

00:09:45.293 --> 00:09:49.088
you could just see the life just be put back into him.

00:09:50.423 --> 00:09:53.801
- [Zack:] Once I got here, everything just kinda got back to normal.

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:57.054
- You know, he rides that dang skateboard.

00:09:57.305 --> 00:10:00.224
- [Mobley:] He's a wild one. He rambunctious or not, he a good guy.

00:10:00.224 --> 00:10:01.183
Real lighthearted.

00:10:01.183 --> 00:10:05.521
- [Stockstill:] He fit in really fast, you know, in the locker room,

00:10:05.521 --> 00:10:08.566
because of his outgoing personality.

00:10:08.691 --> 00:10:11.277
- [Mobley:] Anything he can find to yell about, just to make

00:10:11.277 --> 00:10:13.821
the atmosphere not dead, he does it.

00:10:14.280 --> 00:10:15.698
- But he’s got a great attitude.

00:10:15.698 --> 00:10:18.451
He comes to practice every day to work and get better.

00:10:18.784 --> 00:10:21.078
And if he’ll keep doing that, then he’s got a chance

00:10:21.078 --> 00:10:23.623
to contribute more and more as this season progresses.

00:10:23.956 --> 00:10:24.749
- Look at your body.

00:10:24.832 --> 00:10:26.917
You see that shoulder right there? That’s slowin’ you down. 

00:10:27.001 --> 00:10:28.753
You gotta turn and run.

00:10:28.753 --> 00:10:30.796
You see that? All you gotta do is just run.

00:10:31.088 --> 00:10:32.506
You’re faster than all these dudes.

00:10:33.174 --> 00:10:34.634
OK? Just run. 

00:10:37.303 --> 00:10:39.639
- [Zack:] Before every game, though, I just go into a whole other mode.

00:10:39.639 --> 00:10:41.849
I just think about, just everything that’s happened to me.

00:10:42.516 --> 00:10:44.352
I just be like, “It’s time; it’s time to go.”

00:10:45.311 --> 00:10:47.688
I haven’t scored yet, but when I do score, 

00:10:47.688 --> 00:10:49.815
I always point at the sky or throw my 24s up.

00:10:51.150 --> 00:10:54.570
I’m still a dad, so—like, it’s a blessing really.

00:10:54.570 --> 00:10:57.907
Just reborn again. Like, a new life is born.

00:10:58.240 --> 00:11:00.493
My brother’s name is Zaevion William Dobson. 

00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:02.787
So I, I named him Zion William Dobson.

00:11:03.663 --> 00:11:07.750
- [Anthony:] Zack is still showin’ out as the backflippin’, skateboardin’ life of the party.

00:11:08.501 --> 00:11:12.129
But let’s be real: Zack is more than just a brother of a hero.

00:11:12.755 --> 00:11:14.507
He is more than a boy who ran.

00:11:15.132 --> 00:11:17.718
So I went to Middle Tennessee State to find him because

00:11:17.718 --> 00:11:21.389
I wanted to remind them all: This is what Hoodie Season is.

00:11:22.056 --> 00:11:24.266
- [Stockstill:] Are you a talker or you a doer?

00:11:25.142 --> 00:11:27.895
Are you a man of action or are you a man of words?

